{
  "_doc": "Every move in the energy system (battle/energy.gd, battle/pkmn_battle.gd, design/energy_system.md). id -> name (shown UPPERCASE), type (the move's Pokemon type), category (physical | special | status), role (offense | reaction | two_phase | disruption | utility), cost (energy chips: a list of energy kinds; 'colorless' is paid by any chip, a typed chip pays its own type or a Colorless cost; life/battle_config.json costs.overrides can replace it), power (0 for status), accuracy (0-100; 0 = never misses), priority (higher goes first within a turn), effects (tags: acc_down, atk_down, def_down, def_down2, speed_down, def_up, evasion_up, speed_up, para, burn, sleep, poison, confuse, drain, flinch, high_crit, recoil, trap, force_out, fixed_40, wind, hits_airborne, clear_field, disrupt, sure_hit, identify, break_protect), chance (0-1: how often a damaging move's status effect lands; default in battle_config damage.status_effect_chance), reaction ({trigger: any | physical | special, effect: evade | block | counter, scope: next | turn, mult}), two_phase ({semi: underground | airborne | underwater | charging, on_commit: effects on the commit turn}), anim (the battle's animation key), desc (one line for the move list). Power budget per cost: 1 chip ~35-40, 2 ~70-80, 3 ~115-125, 4 ~170-185; two-phase moves give more per chip (2 chips ~100, 3 ~170). Moves off the user's own types cost Colorless only, with one extra chip.",
  "_schema": {
      "_file": "A move catalog: {\"moves\": {id: move}}. Other catalogs (moves_kanto.json) use the same schema and are merged by id.",
      "id": "lower_snake_case, unique (e.g. thunder_shock).",
      "name": "string, shown UPPERCASE.",
      "type": "the move's Pokemon type: normal fire water electric grass ice fighting poison ground flying psychic bug rock ghost dragon dark steel fairy. Its energy kind is pokemon.json type_energy (normal -> colorless).",
      "category": "physical | special | status.",
      "role": "offense | reaction | two_phase | disruption | utility (required).",
      "tier": "opener (about 1 chip, low focus) | mid (2 to 3 chips; 4 for the heaviest) | finisher (all chips). Alongside role.",
      "cost": "an Array of energy kinds, one per chip, e.g. [\"electric\", \"electric\", \"colorless\"]: a typed chip pays its own kind or a Colorless cost, colorless is paid by any chip. Or a finisher: {\"all\": true, \"min\": N, \"type\": kind | \"any\"}: needs at least N chips (N of that kind unless any) and consumes every unlocked chip. Two-phase moves are paid on the commit turn.",
      "power": "number, 0 for status. A finisher's base power.",
      "power_per_chip": "finisher only: power added per chip spent (battle_config finisher.power_per_chip_default when missing).",
      "accuracy": "0-100; 0 = never misses.",
      "priority": "integer; higher acts first within the turn (reactions 3-4, Quick Attack 1, Roar -1).",
      "effects": "tags: acc_down atk_down def_down def_down2 speed_down def_up evasion_up speed_up para burn sleep poison confuse drain flinch high_crit recoil trap force_out fixed_40 wind hits_airborne clear_field disrupt sure_hit identify break_protect.",
      "chance": "0-1, a damaging move's status effect chance (battle_config damage.status_effect_chance when missing).",
      "reaction": "reaction only: {trigger: any | attack | physical | special, effect: evade | block | counter, scope: next | turn, mult (counter)}.",
      "two_phase": "two_phase only: {semi: underground | airborne | underwater | charging, on_commit: [effect tags]}.",
      "anim": "the battle's animation key.",
      "desc": "one short line for the move list (no em dashes).",
      "budget": "power per cost: 1 chip ~35-40, 2 ~70-80, 3 ~115-125, 4 ~170-185; two-phase more per chip (2 ~100, 3 ~170); a finisher ~20-30 + ~36-38 a chip. Off-type moves cost Colorless only, one extra chip. Interactions (Dig vs Earthquake...) live in battle_config counters.rows, not here."
  },
